  slide "WindowTStarSampler" {
    eyebrow: "WindowTStarSampler"
    title: "Uniform draw in [lo, hi]; collapsed windows skip RNG"
    lede: "`WindowTStarSampler` draws uniformly in `[lo, hi]`. Non-positive duration or `hi ≤ lo` returns an exact instant — float microseconds, no integer truncation."

    narration: "When the trajectory duration is positive and the window upper bound is strictly above the lower bound, t* is a uniform random instant inside that open window. Otherwise the sampler returns an exact instant: zero for a non-positive duration, or the clamped lower bound when the window collapses — including the default ratios that pin both ends at zero."

    term: {
      word: "WindowTStarSampler"
      meaning: "Window policy for t*: t* = uniform(min×dur, max×dur) when the window is open; otherwise an exact instant with no RNG draw."
    }

    points: [
      "Open window: `NumpyPcg64` uniform in `[lo, hi]`, then `t.max(0.0)` — float µs, no integer truncation.",
      "`duration_us ≤ 0` → `0.0`; `hi ≤ lo` → `lo.max(0.0)` with no draw.",
      "Knobs feed the sampler: `trajectory_start_*_ratio` and `t_star_random_seed`.",
      "Evidence: `rust/runtime/src/graph/tstar.rs` — `WindowTStarSampler::sample_t_star`."
    ]

    caption: "Open window draws · collapsed window is exact."

    render: @scene {
      sdk.Header(
        id = "s7-hdr",
        title = "UNIFORM · OR EXACT INSTANT",
        caption = "Open window draws · collapsed window is exact.",
        x = 18, y = 16, width = 664, height = 44,
