  slide "Prompt path unchanged" {
    eyebrow: "Prompt path unchanged"
    title: "Pre-t* segments stay so resume materializes exactly"
    lede: "Topology chops arrivals and edges, but each surviving node's prompt segment program is left unchanged — the full pre-`t*` prefix stays in the path for the exact resume prompt."

    narration: "Dropping early turns from the live graph does not truncate the prompt program on later survivors. Materialization still walks the full segment path including pre-t* history, so the worker builds the same resume prompt the recorded turn would have sent — exact content, not a chopped stub."

    term: {
      word: "unchanged prompt program"
      meaning: "After chop_trie_at_tstar, survivor LlmNode prompt/segment paths still include the full pre-t* prefix so materialization rebuilds the exact resume prompt."
    }

    points: [
      "Chop mutates nodes/edges/inputs — not the survivor's prompt segment program.",
      "Pre-`t*` segments remain in the path (motif: path still lists `n0` · `n1` content).",
      "Exact resume prompt ≠ truncated frontier-only prompt.",
      "Evidence: `rust/runtime/src/graph/snapshot.rs` — \"Leaves each surviving node's prompt segment program unchanged.\""
    ]

    caption: "Live frontier nodes · full historical prompt path."

    render: @scene {
      sdk.Header(
        id = "s11-hdr",
