  slide "Source map" {
    eyebrow: "Source map"
    title: "Where the machinery lives — and the real knobs"
    lede: "Sampler, chop, handoff, and phase resume map to four runtime files. Config knobs are `trajectory_start_min_ratio`, `trajectory_start_max_ratio`, and `t_star_random_seed`."

    narration: "tstar.rs owns duration and window sampling. snapshot.rs owns trie chops and frontier residuals. warmup_handoff.rs defines the payload. graph_phase_runtime.rs drains, builds the handoff, and resumes profiling lanes. Only those three trajectory knobs configure the window and seed — no invented names."

    term: {
      word: "trajectory knobs"
      meaning: "Config v2 fields trajectory_start_min_ratio, trajectory_start_max_ratio, and t_star_random_seed — the real controls for the t* window and lane-salted RNG base."
    }

    points: [
      "`rust/runtime/src/graph/tstar.rs` — window sampler · lane salt · PermutationDraw.",
      "`rust/runtime/src/graph/snapshot.rs` — `chop_trie_at_tstar` · `chop_trie_at_frontier`.",
      "`rust/runtime/src/graph/warmup_handoff.rs` + `engine/graph_phase_runtime.rs` — payload · drain · resume.",
